    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2bb631a3_f88e8436",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 51
      },
      "lineNbr": 189,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T18:09:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This patch is not experimental.\n\n--iteflash_use_ftdi_with_servo_v2\u003dtrue (default value) maintains the existing behavior with Servo v2.\n\n--iteflash_use_ftdi_with_servo_v2\u003dfalse is experimental.  I\u0027ve added an \"EXPERIMENTAL\" warning to the help output.  It works, or did many months ago when I last tested it by first sending the waveform from Servo Micro.  It would be nice to move servo_v2 waveform generation into a servod command at some point.  With that done we could delete the flag, keeping the \"true\" behavior, and then simplify Servod by removing the FTDI close+reopen hackery.\n\n--iteflash_use_cr50_direct_with_ccd\u003dtrue (default value) maintains the existing behavior with CCD.  It is still supported in this patch because i2c-pseudo isn\u0027t checked in yet.  Once i2c-pseudo is checked in and enabled in labstation images, I will delete this flag and keep only the \"false\" behavior.  I\u0027ve added a TODO comment for that.\n\n--iteflash_use_cr50_direct_with_ccd\u003dfalse is *not* experimental, it should work for boards where reflashing via CR50 works at all.  As mentioned I need your time+help to test it.  I was not able to successfully reflash the Bip I have via CR50 yesterday with or without my changes (failed at same place either way), and I can\u0027t spend time troubleshooting it.",
      "parentUuid": "624a274f_8a0c43ff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 189,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "4fe6104052ed9d12a80449c0fbf53cd961554e8b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
