      "writtenOn": "2019-03-11T18:09:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using \u0026\u0026 that way is generally a misuse.  E.g. if it ends up at the bottom of a function, now the function is returning a likely unintended failure value.  And it fails badly when combined with set -e.\n\nAn \"if\" is the proper way.\n\n(Note that || in this manner is not as bad because when the condition is not met, there is a successful return value / exit code.)",
      "parentUuid": "44d3b4ec_b38bc00e",
      "range": {
